                    "title": "\ud83d\udcd0 FinOps Break-Even Formula",
                    "text": {
                        "content": "### When Does Prompt Caching Save Money?\n- **5-min TTL Write (`1.25x`)**: Break-even is **1.28 reads per write** ($1.25 + 0.10R < 1.00(1+R) \\implies R > 0.28$).\n- **1-hr TTL Write (`2.00x`)**: Break-even is **2.11 reads per write**.\n- **Action**: Keep **Cache Read-to-Write Ratio > 3.0** for strong net savings. If ratio `< 1.0`, remove dynamic timestamps from system prompts!",
                        "format": "MARKDOWN",
